            <div xml:id="d1215">

                <pb facs="1217" n="1207" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-19T11:00:00+08:00">May 19, 1949—11 a.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 19—6:34 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>197. Latest information indicates difficulties obtaining adequate shipping may
                    delay completion of Nationalist evacuation of Tsingtao until second half June.
                    Nationalist commander now moving headquarters close to main evacuation point
                    east of Tsingtao.</p>
                <p>Chinese Navy rapidly completing total evacuation.</p>
                <p>Last US naval vessel left docks this morning, all US vessels thus at outer
                    anchorage able move on few minutes’ notice. Shore liberty restricted to 9 p. m.
                    may soon be granted daylight hours only. Reparations [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Preparations</hi>] underway [to] close officers’ and enlisted men [’s]
                    clubs.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 154; repeated OffEmb Canton 58 and to Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
